# Data and large binary outputs
#
# These are ANCHORED (leading slash) on purpose. A pattern whose only slash is a
# trailing one matches at every depth, and git does not descend into an excluded
# directory -- so an unanchored `data/` here would swallow core/phenocycler/data/
# and make that subtree's own `!/data/integration/` negation unreachable. Its tracked
# tracked CSVs would stay tracked (ignore rules never untrack), but every future
# file under it would be silently invisible. Keep the slash.
/data/
pdfs/
*.pdf
*.Rout
gson/
single_cell_analysis/*.h5ad
single_cell_analysis/*.tsv
apps/islet/www/local_images/
apps/islet/www/local_images
local_images/
apps/islet/Channel_names.junior35.bak
apps/islet/www/segmentation_data/
AI_Markdown/
analysis_output/*
islet_analysis/
literature/*
figures/*

# R workspace and environment files
.RData
.Rhistory
apps/islet/.Renviron
apps/islet/.Rprofile
.Renviron
# Filled-in PubApps EnvironmentFile (may hold secrets if AI is re-enabled); template is deploy/env.sh.example
deploy/env.sh

# Organized script directories (duplicates for organization)
scripts/Python/
scripts/R_files/
scripts/Shell_scripts/

# Notebook execution outputs
notebooks/*_executed.ipynb
notebooks/*.png

# App runtime flags
# shiny-server reloads the app when this file's mtime changes; it is a local
# signal, not configuration.
apps/islet/restart.txt
apps/islet/APP_LOADED_FLAG
apps/islet/R/APP_LOADED_FLAG

# Temporary files
tmp/
# Anchored: unanchored, this hid core/phenocycler/docs/HANDOFF_*.md at any depth --
# and the consolidation docs reference those by name.
/HANDOFF*
scratch_recovered*

# Virtual environments and caches
.venv*/
venv*/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Excel and other large source data
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.xlsm

# IDE and local configs
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Tool downloads (large jars)
scripts/tools/

# Vendored third-party code (cloned, not committed; pins and clone commands are indexed in
# docs/EXTERNAL_PACKAGES.md — e.g. external/UniFORM @ 7c33396d)
# Anchored so it cannot shadow a subtree's own external/ directory.
/external/

# Test and agent caches (previously untracked but NOT ignored, so they would have
# been swept into the monorepo by the first `git add -A`)
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.agents/
.codex/

# Large package files
*.deb
*.rpm
scripts/scvi_comparison_results/new_latent_single_cell.npy

# Local Claude Code settings + pipeline run logs
.claude/settings.local.json
logs/

# DeepCell portal access token. Untracked AND unignored until 2026-08-24, so the
# first `git add -A` of the DCT lane would have committed a live credential.
/deepcellToken

# Worker scratch from the parallel build; never committed.
NEEDS.md
FIX.md
BRIEF.md
